# condor_submit_dag sweep_components_keepbis.dag : sweep_components.dag again for the spot bisectors keep_* of
# bisectors_components.txt (remove_bis_spot = 0: the spot keeps the bisector of its MURaM CCF, then the Dumusque
# bisector times the scaling is added: keep_dumusque (1, 0), keep_dumusque_mu (0, 1), keep_palumbo (Palumbo et al.
# 2024)), the same lines of parameters_components.txt. The identification and the filling factors of the parts are
# those of sweep_components.dag (ident and aggregate are not run again: run it first), everything in ${BASE}/components:
#   0. the lists of the jobs of these bisectors only (SCRIPT PRE jobs_components.sh <bisectors>)
#   1. the grids of every Temp, one job per bisector (build_grids_components.sub)
#   2. one job per line and bisector: the simulation of the 5 parts, stats.json of the totals (run_components.sub)
#   3. tables and figures of the totals of these bisectors (collect_components.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
# Not at the same time as sweep_components.dag: the two write the same lists of jobs.
JOB grids    build_grids_components.sub
JOB sets     run_components.sub
JOB collect  collect_components.sub
VARS collect bisectors="keep_dumusque keep_dumusque_mu keep_palumbo"
SCRIPT PRE grids /bin/bash jobs_components.sh keep_dumusque keep_dumusque_mu keep_palumbo
PARENT grids CHILD sets
PARENT sets  CHILD collect
SCRIPT POST sets /bin/true
